WEBVTT

00:09.759 --> 00:13.179
DECEMBER 2020

00:14.264 --> 00:16.933
JINNAM BOXING

01:27.128 --> 01:28.463
Oh, sir.

01:28.546 --> 01:30.048
You need to wear a mask.

01:30.131 --> 01:31.257
Sure. Let's go.

01:31.341 --> 01:33.635
You need to wear a mask to get on the bus.

01:33.718 --> 01:34.594
Let's go.

01:34.677 --> 01:36.638
Now get off, put on a mask, and come back.

01:36.721 --> 01:38.473
How dare you tell me what to do!

01:38.556 --> 01:41.601
- We get penalized--
- What about my mask? That's up to me!

01:41.684 --> 01:44.229
- Don't tell me what to do. Damn it!
- Hey.

01:44.312 --> 01:47.190
Just focus on your driving.
You're just a bus driver!

01:47.273 --> 01:48.108
Damn it.

01:48.191 --> 01:50.443
Please put on a mask and come back, sir.

01:50.527 --> 01:52.070
- Come here!
- Don't do this, sir.

01:52.153 --> 01:54.781
- There are passengers on board.
- Let go! What the hell?

01:54.864 --> 01:56.574
- Let me go, you punk!
- Whoa!

01:56.658 --> 01:58.785
- Let go, damn it.
- I'm sorry.

01:58.868 --> 02:00.453
Who the hell are you?

02:00.537 --> 02:03.081
I'm sorry.
I think you'll have to walk home.

02:03.164 --> 02:06.126
- You little!
- Whoa, I am sorry.

02:06.209 --> 02:07.335
You piece of shit!

02:07.418 --> 02:09.212
- Sorry, sir.
- Hey!

02:09.295 --> 02:10.171
I'm so sorry.

02:11.297 --> 02:12.841
Whoa, I'm sorry.

02:12.924 --> 02:14.467
Don't hurt yourself. I'm sorry.

02:14.551 --> 02:15.802
Damn it!

02:17.762 --> 02:18.930
Damn you!

02:19.848 --> 02:20.849
I am sorry.

02:20.932 --> 02:22.642
This is so annoying, damn it.

02:24.769 --> 02:25.687
I'm sorry, sir.

02:25.770 --> 02:26.938
Sorry, my ass.

02:29.649 --> 02:30.483
Darn it.

02:31.192 --> 02:33.111
Sorry about that.

02:33.194 --> 02:35.029
- Thank you, sir.
- Not a problem.

02:36.948 --> 02:38.575
Thanks to you…

02:38.658 --> 02:40.160
You were so cool.

03:21.951 --> 03:23.661
I'm really sorry.

03:24.162 --> 03:27.123
I had no idea it would go on
for this long either.

03:29.000 --> 03:32.086
I am so sorry for bringing this up.

03:32.170 --> 03:34.756
I'll do whatever I can by next month.

03:35.840 --> 03:39.719
So, can you wait just one month?

03:41.262 --> 03:42.972
I'll pay you back, no matter what.

03:43.806 --> 03:46.726
Yes, I'll figure it out by next month.

03:46.809 --> 03:48.478
Okay, thank you.

04:27.308 --> 04:30.895
BLOODHOUNDS

04:34.065 --> 04:37.026
Amidst the economic downturn
due to COVID-19,

04:37.110 --> 04:41.072
a suspended construction project
threatens the safety of the citizens.

04:41.155 --> 04:44.659
Construction on this building
has been suspended twice

04:44.742 --> 04:46.786
due to a worker's positive COVID-19 test.

04:46.869 --> 04:49.580
The construction company
eventually went bankrupt,

04:49.664 --> 04:52.292
leaving this building an eyesore
for four months.

04:52.375 --> 04:54.752
Seoul must act quickly
to resolve this situation.

05:02.051 --> 05:05.179
In the United States, over 3.5 million
hotel employees were laid off

05:05.263 --> 05:06.681
in the third quarter alone.

05:06.764 --> 05:09.600
I'm saying that for at least
the next three to four years,

05:09.684 --> 05:12.603
no foreign company will look
into acquiring this hotel.

05:12.687 --> 05:15.857
- Even less for domestic companies.
- You make claims as if they're true.

05:15.940 --> 05:18.026
I have many friends
that will become the future leaders

05:18.109 --> 05:19.652
of Korea's top fifty corporations.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.822
I have thoroughly discussed it
with them and reached this conclusion,

05:22.905 --> 05:24.449
so these claims are somewhat true.

05:25.325 --> 05:26.159
Actually,

05:27.201 --> 05:28.536
they are true facts.

05:29.245 --> 05:31.956
You're right to negotiate with me,
Mr. Vice President.

05:32.040 --> 05:32.915
Director Hong.

05:34.083 --> 05:37.337
Our bank has lent
400 billion won for this building.

05:37.837 --> 05:40.715
Saying you will only pay back
300 billion isn't a negotiation.

05:40.798 --> 05:43.176
Shouldn't you bear
some loss in this situation?

05:43.760 --> 05:45.053
How else do you do business?

05:45.720 --> 05:47.013
I am not a businessman

05:47.597 --> 05:48.723
but a banker.

05:49.307 --> 05:51.476
Well, Mr. Director and Mr. Vice President,

05:51.976 --> 05:53.811
the reason I gathered
the two of you here--

05:53.895 --> 05:54.729
Yes.

05:54.812 --> 05:58.024
The mayor wants the building
to be completed as soon as possible

05:58.107 --> 05:59.400
for the citizens' safety.

05:59.484 --> 06:01.361
But it's like talking to a brick wall!

06:01.444 --> 06:04.697
Are you calling me a brick wall,
Mr. Vice President?

06:04.781 --> 06:07.116
Just what part of what you said
is reasonable?

06:15.625 --> 06:17.293
I must apologize for being late.

06:18.544 --> 06:21.714
This is CEO Kim Myeong-gil,
who I mentioned before the meal.

06:22.215 --> 06:23.257
Please welcome him.

06:23.341 --> 06:26.928
Assemblyman Seo Woo-hyeon,
a close acquaintance of the mayor,

06:27.011 --> 06:28.596
introduced him to us.

06:29.347 --> 06:30.598
I'm Kim Myeong-gil.

06:32.767 --> 06:34.852
KIM MYEONG-GIL

06:35.937 --> 06:37.814
I'll personally call you later.

06:38.439 --> 06:39.273
Okay.

06:44.028 --> 06:45.029
I'm Kim Myeong-gil.

06:55.706 --> 06:58.126
May I ask what kind of work
you do exactly?

06:59.127 --> 07:00.878
I mainly deal in investments.

07:00.962 --> 07:05.258
When good people ask for me,
I help them to the best of my abilities.

07:05.758 --> 07:08.052
Wait. Do you run a loan business?

07:09.095 --> 07:12.223
Hold on. You brought a loan shark here?

07:13.141 --> 07:15.476
Mr. Kim dabbles in various businesses.

07:15.560 --> 07:18.020
This isn't a place
for a loan shark, is it?

07:20.398 --> 07:23.109
You must be Chairman Hong Woo-geun's
eldest son.

07:24.360 --> 07:27.447
When I was young, I worked
for Chairman Bang in Myeong-dong.

07:27.530 --> 07:30.575
You would not remember this
since you were a baby back then.

07:30.658 --> 07:32.785
When the IMF crisis hit Korea,

07:32.869 --> 07:35.788
Iil Group, a fifty-year-old company,
nearly went bankrupt

07:35.872 --> 07:37.498
because they didn't have six billion won.

07:37.999 --> 07:40.168
Back then, Chairman Hong Woo-geun

07:40.251 --> 07:43.463
visited my boss,
Chairman Bang, asking for help.

07:43.546 --> 07:47.550
He got down on his knees, saying that
he had to save the company at all costs.

07:47.633 --> 07:51.762
Chairman Bang was moved
by his passion and sincerity.

07:53.097 --> 07:57.852
I filled a bag with six billion won
in cash and went to your house.

07:58.644 --> 08:00.688
I recall your mother preparing

08:00.771 --> 08:03.733
refreshing Korean melons for me
to express her gratitude.

08:05.193 --> 08:08.070
Dirty money doesn't exist.
It may be used for nefarious reasons,

08:08.154 --> 08:10.740
but when used for good,
that makes it good money.

08:11.324 --> 08:14.202
I came here to help.

08:17.955 --> 08:20.458
If you'd tell me where we are
in the negotiations…

08:21.125 --> 08:23.878
Each of them had
different amounts in mind.

08:23.961 --> 08:27.215
- We were discussing that.
- I see. How much are we talking?

08:27.298 --> 08:28.883
A hundred billion won.

08:33.095 --> 08:36.599
Do you plan on overseeing
hotel operations yourself, Mr. Hong?

08:37.099 --> 08:39.852
I got my master's degree
in hotel management in Switzerland

08:39.936 --> 08:41.437
and worked for 4 years in Hong Kong.

08:41.521 --> 08:43.648
I see. You are well-prepared.

08:45.358 --> 08:48.444
With your permission,
I'd like to make an investment.

08:50.404 --> 08:51.239
How much?

08:51.322 --> 08:55.785
Well, since you are 100 billion short,
I should invest that much.

08:59.330 --> 09:02.124
I will invest more if you need.

09:02.208 --> 09:03.167
And your terms?

09:03.251 --> 09:05.920
There are only three things.

09:06.504 --> 09:12.176
Firstly, I would like a small casino built
on the top floor of the hotel.

09:12.260 --> 09:14.804
Just as you dream of managing a hotel,

09:14.887 --> 09:17.431
I dream of opening a casino.

09:18.432 --> 09:23.563
Secondly, please help me
set up a small bar in the hotel basement.

09:23.646 --> 09:27.358
Lastly, should something like COVID-19
spread again at a later time,

09:27.441 --> 09:30.820
please open up our hotel
as a quarantine space

09:30.903 --> 09:33.406
for those without money, free of charge.

09:34.490 --> 09:38.494
The harder the times,
the more we should care for each other.

09:38.578 --> 09:41.747
That is how we make a better world.

09:46.043 --> 09:47.712
I am ready

09:48.546 --> 09:50.965
to make my 100 billion investment
as early as tomorrow.

10:07.607 --> 10:08.566
Did it go well?

10:09.984 --> 10:11.819
- Yeah.
- You think they'll take the bait?

10:12.987 --> 10:15.740
- Yeah.
- All right!

10:16.407 --> 10:20.286
Nice! I guess I just need
to worry about how to decorate the bar.

10:20.369 --> 10:22.913
People don't go to bars
to admire the interior design.

10:22.997 --> 10:24.540
They go to see the girls.

10:24.624 --> 10:27.043
You should get busy
recruiting plenty of pretty girls.

10:27.126 --> 10:29.128
You get busy, you fucker.

10:29.211 --> 10:32.214
It'd be nice if someone
as pretty as you could talk nicely too.

10:32.298 --> 10:34.884
What would you know? You prick!

10:37.637 --> 10:39.013
I want to wipe my face.

10:39.597 --> 10:40.431
Right.

10:43.392 --> 10:44.226
Here.

10:59.742 --> 11:00.785
Drive.

11:05.206 --> 11:06.707
What about the Seongeun building?

11:06.791 --> 11:10.002
None of the tenants have any ties
to the police or prosecutor's office.

11:10.086 --> 11:11.379
Including their in-laws?

11:11.462 --> 11:14.340
Sir, I overlooked that just that one time.

11:14.423 --> 11:16.550
One of their lovers might be a cop.

11:16.634 --> 11:18.552
Do your job right, so he doesn't worry.

11:18.636 --> 11:20.930
Jesus, you worry about yourself.

11:21.013 --> 11:22.098
Jang-do,

11:23.182 --> 11:25.601
you should talk respectfully
to your sister-in-law.

11:26.894 --> 11:28.604
Yes, I'm sorry, sir.

11:28.688 --> 11:30.606
Apologize to me, you stupid prick!

11:31.524 --> 11:33.734
This prick apologizes, ma'am.

11:33.818 --> 11:36.487
Let's hurry up.
I could really use a drink.

11:36.570 --> 11:37.405
Yes, sir.

11:40.491 --> 11:43.536
This is the 2020 KBFC
Rookie of the Year Tournament.

11:43.619 --> 11:45.663
The arena should be filled
with cheering fans

11:45.746 --> 11:48.290
showing their support,
but due to the COVID-19 pandemic,

11:48.374 --> 11:50.918
it is being held without any spectators.

11:51.001 --> 11:52.378
The atmosphere feels gloomy.

11:52.461 --> 11:54.797
Yes. The tournament
normally has a lot of cheering

11:54.880 --> 11:58.008
for everyone involved,
but things are quiet right now.

11:58.092 --> 12:01.303
As we speak, we begin
the third round of Hong Woo-jin's match.

12:01.387 --> 12:02.972
It's a middleweight match.

12:03.055 --> 12:04.598
Hong Woo-jin is in the red trunks,

12:04.682 --> 12:06.684
against Jung Jae-hun in the blue trunks.

12:06.767 --> 12:07.601
Get in there.

12:07.685 --> 12:09.562
- Great combination of body shots.
- Yes.

12:09.645 --> 12:10.980
Hong leans against the ropes.

12:11.063 --> 12:13.733
He provokes his opponent
after landing body shots.

12:13.816 --> 12:16.277
Wow, that is right.
He's showing composure.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.903
- "Hit me if you can."
- Yes.

12:17.987 --> 12:19.321
"You can certainly…"

12:19.405 --> 12:20.239
Whoa, a body shot!

12:20.322 --> 12:21.157
There you go.

12:21.240 --> 12:24.285
- A clean hit to the body.
- And he just landed a blow to the face!

12:24.368 --> 12:26.537
He knocks his opponent down! Hong Woo-jin!

12:26.620 --> 12:29.039
Whoa, that double right
followed by a one-two combo.

12:29.123 --> 12:31.959
Yes, look at that footwork.
He has great showmanship.

12:32.042 --> 12:33.294
Whoa, it's a KO.

12:33.836 --> 12:37.465
Next, we have Kim Gun-woo
going up against Kim Rae-hyeon.

12:37.548 --> 12:39.550
We have super rookie Kim Gun-woo in blue.

12:39.633 --> 12:42.511
Kim Gun-woo is looking
for a chance with his guard up.

12:42.595 --> 12:43.512
Nice!

12:43.596 --> 12:45.556
- A body blow!
- He goes down on his knees!

12:45.639 --> 12:48.142
That's right.
A precision blow to the solar plexus…

12:48.225 --> 12:50.186
- And that is the end of the match.
- Indeed.

12:50.269 --> 12:51.729
That one blow ended the match.

12:51.812 --> 12:54.940
Kim Gun-woo continues to mow down
his opponents with a single blow.

12:55.024 --> 12:56.400
- He is a flawless boxer.
- Nice job.

12:56.484 --> 12:58.068
A terrifying rookie has emerged.

12:58.652 --> 13:00.446
Things are already getting heated.

13:00.529 --> 13:02.740
- He's cornered.
- He's getting cornered.

13:05.242 --> 13:08.245
He grabs him and throws him over.
He just threw his opponent down.

13:08.329 --> 13:09.872
That was a foul.

13:09.955 --> 13:11.665
- That's right.
- He did it first…

13:11.749 --> 13:13.375
- He's too agitated.
- Right.

13:13.459 --> 13:15.044
- Box!
- Let's do this!

13:15.544 --> 13:18.297
How he parts his hair.
Hong's showmanship is unmatched.

13:18.380 --> 13:20.257
- I agree.
- He provokes his opponent first.

13:20.341 --> 13:21.342
He dodges.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.260
Whoa, look at him dodge!

13:25.763 --> 13:27.807
And again.
He connects! We have a knockout!

13:27.890 --> 13:29.850
That is Hong Woo-jin's specialty.

13:29.934 --> 13:32.144
- Right.
- A double jab followed by a straight!

13:32.228 --> 13:33.979
Hong Woo-jin, the Marine.

13:34.063 --> 13:36.398
Hong Woo-jin advances yet again.

13:37.358 --> 13:39.860
Now, a match between
Kim Gun-woo and Lee Yong-gyu.

13:41.821 --> 13:44.365
Kim Gun-woo in the red trunks
is built like a tank.

13:44.448 --> 13:45.783
- That's right.
- Nice dodge.

13:45.866 --> 13:48.452
- Kim Gun-woo's strength is in infighting.
- Right.

13:48.536 --> 13:51.372
He is leveraging
his infighting skills well.

13:51.455 --> 13:53.541
Another punch, and he dodges.

13:53.624 --> 13:56.836
- Body shot!
- He brings him down with one blow again!

13:56.919 --> 13:59.088
- Yes, a left hook to the body.
- Yes.

13:59.171 --> 14:01.382
I also had that level of talent
back in the day.

14:01.465 --> 14:03.551
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

14:03.634 --> 14:06.053
- That's why you won a gold medal.
- That is true.

14:06.887 --> 14:08.514
Now, Kim Gun-woo versus Hong Woo-jin.

14:08.597 --> 14:11.267
- All right.
- Let's find out who takes home the trophy.

14:11.350 --> 14:14.019
No big moves.
Short punches. Use your waist!

14:14.103 --> 14:16.856
Watch out for his left hook.
His punches are no joke.

14:23.737 --> 14:26.240
Hey, I'm a Marine.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.492
Watch out for his left hook.

14:28.576 --> 14:30.911
I'm an invincible Marine. Invincible!

14:30.995 --> 14:34.081
If he beats the shit out of you
and you cry, I'm going to kill you.

14:39.044 --> 14:40.254
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

14:43.632 --> 14:45.801
Good luck to you both. To your corners.

14:49.972 --> 14:51.891
His fighting so far has been marvelous.

14:51.974 --> 14:55.686
Kim Gun-woo, the super rookie,
has a very different fighting style.

14:55.769 --> 14:59.440
That's right. Kim Gun-woo is an infighter
who's good against other infighters.

14:59.523 --> 15:00.983
Right.

15:01.066 --> 15:06.030
On the other hand, Hong Woo-jin is
an out boxer with a counter up his sleeve.

15:06.113 --> 15:09.116
That's right, Hong Woo-jin knows
how to have fun in his matches.

15:09.199 --> 15:10.034
Right.

15:10.117 --> 15:13.037
Meanwhile, his opponent,
who stoically plays it by the book…

15:13.120 --> 15:15.831
He's going in! He's cornering him!

15:15.915 --> 15:18.500
Can Hong Woo-jin get out?
Can he get out of this?

15:18.584 --> 15:20.002
He got out of that really well.

15:20.085 --> 15:24.131
- Yes, Hong Woo-jin is really fast.
- That's right.

15:24.214 --> 15:26.425
Since Kim Gun-woo is also a middleweight--

15:26.508 --> 15:28.594
And now he goes for a wild swing!

15:29.720 --> 15:31.055
- Yes.
- Blocked that. Body blows.

15:31.138 --> 15:33.015
Kim Gun-woo has a great defense.

15:33.098 --> 15:35.351
- Yes.
- He's like a solid rock.

15:35.434 --> 15:37.770
He keeps his guard up.

15:37.853 --> 15:38.687
Uppercut!

15:38.771 --> 15:40.481
- There we go.
- He landed that one.

15:40.564 --> 15:42.149
Yes, indeed.

15:42.232 --> 15:43.484
What a performance this is.

15:43.567 --> 15:44.902
A right hook! What a dodge.

15:44.985 --> 15:46.862
Now it's Hong Woo-jin's turn.

15:46.946 --> 15:50.074
Hong Woo-jin is
constantly applying pressure.

15:50.908 --> 15:53.827
- Another left hook to the body!
- A left hook. Can he recover?

15:53.911 --> 15:55.996
- He goes down.
- He's down!

15:56.080 --> 15:57.039
He's down.

15:57.706 --> 16:01.085
Yes, when it comes to stomach blows,
the shock does not immediately set in.

16:01.168 --> 16:03.712
- Right.
- It takes around five seconds.

16:03.796 --> 16:04.797
Get up! Woo-jin!

16:04.880 --> 16:06.340
Six, seven…

16:06.423 --> 16:07.967
- He's up in five seconds.
- Right.

16:08.050 --> 16:09.802
- He recovered from that well.
- He did…

16:09.885 --> 16:10.803
Yes.

16:10.886 --> 16:12.930
But that has definitely got to sting.

16:13.013 --> 16:15.307
- There's going to be an aftereffect.
- Right.

16:17.226 --> 16:18.060
Come on.

16:20.145 --> 16:22.606
Come on!

16:48.173 --> 16:49.008
Come on.

16:49.800 --> 16:52.052
Hey, come and get some.

16:54.221 --> 16:55.472
You son of a bitch.

16:57.891 --> 16:59.893
I said come on!

17:01.770 --> 17:03.105
Will he take the bait?

17:03.188 --> 17:05.357
- Kim Gun-woo has a lot to think about.
- Come on!

17:05.441 --> 17:07.735
And there he goes! Will he connect?

17:07.818 --> 17:11.155
Stop! One, two…

17:11.238 --> 17:13.574
It must have done significant damage.

17:13.657 --> 17:15.409
His tactics really backfired.

17:15.492 --> 17:16.410
That's correct.

17:16.493 --> 17:19.121
Kim Gun-woo went in for the kill
and ended the match

17:19.204 --> 17:24.293
once again with the same body blow.

17:28.464 --> 17:29.590
Are you all right?

17:30.257 --> 17:32.843
I have stained the honor of the Marines.

17:33.594 --> 17:35.512
Everyone goes down
after a blow to the liver.

17:36.722 --> 17:37.639
I'm leaving.

17:38.640 --> 17:39.892
Aren't we gonna eat?

17:40.684 --> 17:41.810
There's COVID-19 going on.

17:42.394 --> 17:45.564
I've just gone through a lot.
The least you can do is feed me.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.915
Go home and order takeout.

18:06.126 --> 18:06.960
See you.

18:23.227 --> 18:24.853
What? Why? What?

18:25.854 --> 18:26.855
Shall we go eat?

18:27.606 --> 18:29.274
Why would I eat with you?

18:29.858 --> 18:32.861
I was going to have pork belly.
I thought we could eat together.

18:35.531 --> 18:36.573
Are you pitying me?

18:37.157 --> 18:37.991
No.

18:38.075 --> 18:40.202
Go ask those other bastards you KO'd.

18:40.285 --> 18:41.912
They all went home.

18:43.122 --> 18:44.248
Damn it.

18:56.677 --> 18:59.304
- Isn't the prize money ten million won?
- Yes.

19:00.264 --> 19:03.392
Then why eat pork belly?
Let's get some rib eye.

19:03.475 --> 19:06.145
- I'm only going to spend 50,000 won.
- Why?

19:06.228 --> 19:07.980
I need to give the rest to my mom.

19:08.063 --> 19:10.107
- Do you owe your mom money?
- No.

19:10.190 --> 19:11.066
Then why?

19:11.567 --> 19:13.527
I have to pay the rent for her café.

19:14.361 --> 19:15.404
You're a good son.

19:16.280 --> 19:17.614
Spend an additional 10,000 won.

19:17.698 --> 19:20.284
There's a barbecue buffet
that charges 29,000 won per person.

19:20.367 --> 19:22.035
Top quality. They have Korean beef.

19:22.119 --> 19:24.204
- Really? Where?
- I'm kidding, you chump.

19:25.581 --> 19:27.916
How can they afford
to serve Korean beef for 29,000 won?

19:28.584 --> 19:30.294
Have you spent
your entire life just boxing?

19:31.461 --> 19:33.881
That buffet is all right.
Just spend 10,000 won more.

19:33.964 --> 19:34.798
No.

19:37.301 --> 19:38.135
Hey.

19:48.061 --> 19:48.896
Let's go.

19:50.480 --> 19:51.940
How is your left hook so strong?

19:52.441 --> 19:56.028
I practiced on a tire
when I worked part-time at a junkyard.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.279
Just your left hook?

19:58.488 --> 19:59.781
Why only work on my left hook?

19:59.865 --> 20:01.867
I'm asking
if you only worked on your left.

20:01.950 --> 20:03.785
I practiced both.

20:03.869 --> 20:05.537
Then how's your left so strong?

20:05.621 --> 20:08.874
- My right hand is stronger.
- Then why did you only use your left?

20:08.957 --> 20:11.293
I couldn't find the right timing
for my right.

20:12.711 --> 20:13.545
What a show-off.

20:14.588 --> 20:15.422
How so?

20:15.505 --> 20:18.258
You're saying you could take
everyone down with your left.

20:18.342 --> 20:19.468
Today, yes.

20:19.551 --> 20:21.386
See? You are a show-off.

20:21.970 --> 20:24.306
- No, I'm totally humble.
- Just flip the meat.

20:24.389 --> 20:26.308
We have to give it another 30 seconds.

20:26.391 --> 20:28.143
You can flip it right now.

20:28.227 --> 20:31.355
No, I worked part-time
at a barbecue place. I know my meat.

20:31.438 --> 20:33.607
Jeez. You sure
worked a lot of part-time jobs.

20:34.107 --> 20:37.069
- Are you poor?
- Yes, our family went broke.

20:39.488 --> 20:40.405
How?

20:42.866 --> 20:45.244
My dad was a researcher
for a large corporation.

20:45.327 --> 20:48.455
He sued for wrongful termination
but lost four years later.

20:48.997 --> 20:51.250
The legal fees
from back then turned into debt.

20:52.251 --> 20:54.753
You can't beat the big companies.
The rich always win.

20:54.836 --> 20:55.879
That's true.

20:58.715 --> 21:01.551
- What else did you do part-time?
- All sorts of things.

21:01.635 --> 21:03.553
But I mostly went on
delivery runs with my mom.

21:04.888 --> 21:06.848
You're a world-class part-timer.

21:08.850 --> 21:10.018
Whoa.

21:10.519 --> 21:13.021
You're good at everything.
You've led a good life.

21:13.522 --> 21:15.107
I see you grill right handed.

21:16.233 --> 21:17.567
When did you start boxing?

21:18.277 --> 21:20.195
About three years ago.

21:20.279 --> 21:22.281
- When was that?
- After my military service.

21:22.364 --> 21:23.407
I see.

21:24.074 --> 21:26.243
I first put on boxing gloves
in sixth grade.

21:26.326 --> 21:27.995
My dad was on the national team.

21:28.078 --> 21:31.540
That is awesome. What is your dad's name?

21:31.623 --> 21:34.501
Hong Seong-geun.
The Barcelona Olympics Bronze medalist.

21:34.584 --> 21:36.169
- I see.
- Do you know him?

21:36.253 --> 21:37.379
No.

21:38.463 --> 21:40.048
Most boxers seem to know him.

21:40.132 --> 21:42.134
I see. Sorry.

21:43.593 --> 21:45.429
Did your dad teach you how to box?

21:46.263 --> 21:48.765
- I'm not that close to my dad.
- Why not?

21:49.433 --> 21:51.643
My dad is never satisfied
with anything I do.

21:52.144 --> 21:56.481
He won his bronze medal at my age and
judges me based on his accomplishments.

21:59.651 --> 22:04.948
Then did your dad win
that bronze medal when he was twenty-five?

22:06.074 --> 22:07.617
No, twenty-seven.

22:10.746 --> 22:12.247
How old are you?

22:12.831 --> 22:14.041
Twenty-seven.

22:14.624 --> 22:16.668
Well, I apologize, then.

22:16.752 --> 22:18.879
I'm twenty-five. I am so sorry.

22:18.962 --> 22:20.756
Jeez. You little bastard.

22:20.839 --> 22:21.673
Forgive me.

22:21.757 --> 22:22.799
- Hey.
- Yes?

22:22.883 --> 22:24.593
Behave from now on, okay?

22:24.676 --> 22:25.927
- Will do.
- Got it?

22:26.470 --> 22:27.304
Yes.

22:27.971 --> 22:28.889
Flip it.

22:28.972 --> 22:31.266
No, it still needs a minute.

22:31.350 --> 22:33.435
- It's fine. Flip it!
- I can't do that.

22:33.518 --> 22:37.147
Jeez! You're one stubborn punk.
Have you served in the army yet?

22:37.230 --> 22:40.192
Yes, I told you I started boxing
after I finished my service.

22:40.275 --> 22:41.568
I know.

22:41.651 --> 22:43.987
What I'm asking is,
where were you stationed?

22:44.071 --> 22:47.240
- You should catch on quicker.
- I was in the Marine Corps.

22:48.450 --> 22:49.451
Hey!

22:50.035 --> 22:51.578
I am a Marine too!

22:51.661 --> 22:52.579
I see.

22:52.662 --> 22:53.872
What class were you in?

22:53.955 --> 22:56.041
I was in the 1,207th class.

22:58.377 --> 23:01.004
Salute! I was in the 1,216th class, sir!

23:01.088 --> 23:03.840
What are you doing? Please sit.

23:03.924 --> 23:06.927
- I will sit when you return my salute.
- Right. Well…

23:10.472 --> 23:11.973
Marine Kim Gun-woo, sir.

23:12.057 --> 23:13.767
- Yes?
- Where did you serve, sir?

23:14.393 --> 23:15.227
The First Division.

23:15.310 --> 23:17.229
Me too! Which battalion were you in, sir?

23:18.438 --> 23:20.732
- Reconnaissance.
- Amazing.

23:21.400 --> 23:24.361
I wanted to get into reconnaissance,
but I didn't make the cut.

23:24.444 --> 23:27.072
- I see.
- The pride of the Marines, recon.

23:27.614 --> 23:28.448
Recon!

23:30.784 --> 23:33.453
I'll call you bro,
so let's just speak casually.

23:34.371 --> 23:35.622
I understand, sir.

23:35.705 --> 23:36.998
Let's be casual.

23:37.082 --> 23:38.542
Casual it is, sir.

23:38.625 --> 23:39.584
Brother.

23:41.044 --> 23:41.878
Here.

23:45.048 --> 23:49.219
I have a crazy amount
of pride as a Marine.

23:49.302 --> 23:50.137
Why?

23:50.220 --> 23:52.722
I used to be a bit of a thug in Incheon,

23:52.806 --> 23:55.725
but I joined the Marine Corps
and met some really nice people.

23:55.809 --> 23:57.185
Now I've finally come to my senses.

23:57.269 --> 24:01.440
I loved training and overcoming
all the difficulties together.

24:01.523 --> 24:02.774
This looks delicious.

24:02.858 --> 24:05.360
Waking up in the morning,
going on runs, sweating,

24:05.444 --> 24:06.987
showering and washing each other.

24:07.070 --> 24:08.738
- Woo-jin.
- Yes?

24:10.115 --> 24:12.451
- Are you one of those crazy Marines?
- Of course not.

24:12.534 --> 24:13.702
Try this.

24:16.288 --> 24:17.247
How is it?

24:19.583 --> 24:21.126
It's practically steak.

24:21.209 --> 24:22.043
Really?

24:23.670 --> 24:24.754
Check this out.

24:26.006 --> 24:27.215
- Three pieces.
- Whoa, yes.

24:27.299 --> 24:29.259
- With some ssamjang.
- Yes.

24:29.342 --> 24:30.677
And kimchi with that too?

24:35.056 --> 24:37.017
- Marine Kim Gun-woo, sir.
- Yes?

24:41.313 --> 24:43.064
- It's amazing, isn't it?
- Yes.

24:43.607 --> 24:44.983
- Do you want some soju?
- No.

24:45.066 --> 24:46.943
- Why? Because of your diet?
- Yes.

24:47.027 --> 24:49.237
You perfectionist. So annoying.

24:50.363 --> 24:52.616
Excuse me!

24:52.699 --> 24:55.744
A bottle of beer and soju, please!

24:57.454 --> 24:59.080
How much did your shoes cost?

24:59.581 --> 25:00.999
- 1,200,000 won.
- Really?

25:02.000 --> 25:04.127
Why so expensive?
That's rent for our café.

25:04.211 --> 25:05.795
How are you so gullible?

25:05.879 --> 25:07.506
They're knockoffs.

25:09.049 --> 25:10.133
They look real.

25:10.217 --> 25:12.802
Knockoffs have shiny toe caps.

25:12.886 --> 25:15.972
The real ones are suede.
The finishing on the holes is shoddy too.

25:17.098 --> 25:19.601
I can find one for you
that's better than the real deal.

25:19.684 --> 25:21.853
- Really?
- I can't believe this guy.

25:21.937 --> 25:25.106
Nothing in this world tops the real deal.

25:26.149 --> 25:28.818
You should hang out with me
and learn about the world.

25:28.902 --> 25:31.196
I think you've been working too much.

25:33.281 --> 25:36.117
Do you know about this?
I hear it's very common nowadays.

25:37.577 --> 25:39.329
"COVID-19 special loans."

25:40.163 --> 25:43.833
Back then, I was strapped for cash,
so I worked in the money-lending business.

25:43.917 --> 25:47.587
- Yes.
- Desperate people are easier to rip off.

25:47.671 --> 25:49.965
The pandemic has made
a lot of people desperate.

25:52.175 --> 25:55.887
- The loan sharks are so damn excited.
- How come?

25:55.971 --> 25:58.807
Since everyone is rushing over
to cover their rent,

25:58.890 --> 26:02.686
all they need to do
is sit still and suck them dry.

26:03.395 --> 26:06.565
My mom is having a hard time
because of the rent at the café.

26:07.315 --> 26:09.859
The café makes less than a quarter
of what it used to,

26:09.943 --> 26:12.153
but the landlord still takes
the same amount of rent.

26:13.613 --> 26:16.199
If we close down now,
it would cost us more to move out.

26:16.283 --> 26:17.826
So we're just holding on.

26:17.909 --> 26:20.537
They say we need to restore it
to its original state.

26:22.205 --> 26:23.206
Damn.

26:26.793 --> 26:27.627
Here.

26:29.796 --> 26:32.257
I will treat you
to something real fancy next time.

26:33.300 --> 26:34.134
Rib eye?

26:34.217 --> 26:36.970
There is a butcher's shop
and barbecue place.

26:37.053 --> 26:38.305
You're not lying, are you?

26:38.388 --> 26:42.934
Do you think I'd tell a senior Marine
such a low-level fib?

26:43.018 --> 26:45.395
- I think you totally would.
- You don't believe me?

26:45.478 --> 26:47.897
You kept lying to me earlier.

26:47.981 --> 26:50.775
Jeez. That was a joke, you fool.

26:50.859 --> 26:52.569
All right, no more lies going forward.

26:53.862 --> 26:54.696
Deal.

26:55.864 --> 26:59.075
I am so sorry.

26:59.159 --> 27:02.621
I should've prepared it this month,

27:03.121 --> 27:04.748
but I was not able to.

27:05.498 --> 27:09.794
Yes, I'll try to figure something out
after this month.

27:11.129 --> 27:12.213
I am sorry.

27:14.049 --> 27:15.967
- Sorry, let me call you back.
- Mom.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.302
I'll call in the morning.

27:18.136 --> 27:19.596
My son!

27:20.347 --> 27:21.931
Oh my God!

27:23.892 --> 27:25.935
You were amazing today!

27:26.019 --> 27:28.480
- You watched it?
- Of course I did.

27:28.563 --> 27:30.857
The commentators complimented you so much.

27:30.940 --> 27:33.777
- Really?
- Yes, they said you were flawless.

27:33.860 --> 27:35.236
Then I should watch it too.

27:36.154 --> 27:37.739
- Mom, hold on.
- Yes.

27:37.822 --> 27:39.157
I am so proud of you.

27:40.200 --> 27:41.326
Here.

27:42.202 --> 27:43.161
What is this?

27:43.870 --> 27:45.997
The prize money. Pay your rent with it.

27:48.333 --> 27:49.417
Jeez.

27:50.001 --> 27:51.836
I can't take this.

27:53.588 --> 27:55.423
No, I won this to give to you.

27:59.010 --> 28:02.389
Let's pay off the money
we borrowed from Uncle first.

28:02.472 --> 28:03.348
What?

28:04.557 --> 28:06.601
How do you know about that?

28:06.685 --> 28:09.979
Uncle is having a hard time too.
Let's hurry and pay him back.

28:14.609 --> 28:15.568
Okay.

28:16.653 --> 28:19.489
I'll make sure
to pay you back with interest.

28:19.572 --> 28:22.575
- Okay.
- Thank you.

28:26.287 --> 28:27.414
Let's go, Mom.

28:27.497 --> 28:29.082
Jeez, it's so cold. Let's go.

28:29.999 --> 28:31.292
Did you eat?

28:31.376 --> 28:32.335
Yes, of course.

28:32.419 --> 28:33.795
With who?

28:34.379 --> 28:36.548
The guy I fought in the finals.

28:37.507 --> 28:40.802
The boy with the curly hair?

28:40.885 --> 28:41.845
Yes, him.

28:43.930 --> 28:45.056
Mom, did you eat?

28:45.140 --> 28:46.516
Yes, I ate too.

29:05.201 --> 29:06.035
Sir.

29:06.619 --> 29:07.537
How are things?

29:08.413 --> 29:11.750
All tenants owe money to banks
or second-tier financial companies,

29:11.833 --> 29:12.834
as you said, sir.

29:13.585 --> 29:16.629
I will bring them all
to our company next week.

29:16.713 --> 29:19.549
Can you make it happen this week?

29:20.175 --> 29:22.969
Assemblyman Seo keeps badgering me
to kick them out fast.

29:24.471 --> 29:25.513
I'll get it done, sir.

29:25.597 --> 29:27.724
Yes, let's hurry things up.

29:28.224 --> 29:30.268
Jun-min, the sales team
is the most important.

29:31.060 --> 29:31.895
Yes, sir.

29:36.483 --> 29:37.567
Beom.

29:39.652 --> 29:40.612
Let's get ready.

30:00.215 --> 30:03.301
I'm the team manager, Yoo In-yeong,
from Smile Capital.

30:03.885 --> 30:05.595
We are a financial company

30:05.678 --> 30:07.806
that has been government-certified
for excellence.

30:07.889 --> 30:12.143
- Do you have a moment to talk?
- Sure.

30:12.811 --> 30:15.897
There haven't been
many customers here lately, right?

30:17.398 --> 30:18.316
No.

30:18.399 --> 30:21.152
Sir, you have a bank loan
of 40 million won, right?

30:21.778 --> 30:22.612
Yes.

30:22.695 --> 30:27.075
Once you sign here,
we will pay off that debt today.

30:27.158 --> 30:31.412
We have a 5% interest rate,
which is lower than the bank's 7%.

30:31.496 --> 30:34.374
Then, how do you turn a profit?

30:34.457 --> 30:35.416
Well, that's true.

30:35.500 --> 30:38.962
But the government has started
a special support program

30:39.045 --> 30:43.091
to help small business owners
who are struggling from the pandemic.

30:43.174 --> 30:47.136
We won the bid for the support package,
which lets us lower our interest rates.

30:47.220 --> 30:50.098
A 2% interest rate is not a small amount.

30:50.723 --> 30:53.768
In times like this,
you win if you hold out.

30:55.603 --> 30:58.189
COVID-19? This too shall pass.

30:58.731 --> 31:02.777
We'd like to help
so you can continue running your business.

31:05.363 --> 31:07.031
This is good for us,

31:07.115 --> 31:09.325
but it's beneficial for you too, sir.

31:12.370 --> 31:14.831
- Thank you.
- I should be the one thanking you.

31:14.914 --> 31:16.332
SMILE CAPITAL
SIGNEE YOON SO-YEON

31:20.795 --> 31:22.881
SPARK BOXING GYM

31:32.557 --> 31:33.516
What?

31:33.600 --> 31:35.018
TEMPORARILY CLOSED

31:35.101 --> 31:38.897
Some members at the gym
ordered some fried chicken last night.

31:38.980 --> 31:41.357
Apparently, one of them tested positive.

31:42.066 --> 31:44.152
Should I get tested too?

31:44.652 --> 31:45.486
You're fine.

31:45.570 --> 31:50.074
Anyway, your match was just yesterday.
Why did you come to the gym?

31:50.158 --> 31:52.535
- To work out.
- Gun-woo.

31:53.202 --> 31:54.329
Take a week off.

31:54.954 --> 31:56.205
And do what?

31:56.289 --> 31:58.499
You're not resting
if you're doing something.

31:59.000 --> 32:00.752
Don't do anything and just rest.

32:01.502 --> 32:02.337
Okay.

32:12.847 --> 32:15.183
GU-NOO

32:22.941 --> 32:24.525
Hey, what are you up to?

32:26.319 --> 32:27.528
Sleeping.

32:27.612 --> 32:28.655
What?

32:28.738 --> 32:30.031
Sleeping.

32:31.115 --> 32:32.241
I can't hear you.

32:32.325 --> 32:33.576
I said I'm sleeping.

32:33.660 --> 32:35.954
I am sleeping.

32:36.621 --> 32:38.414
Do you want to work out?

32:38.498 --> 32:40.291
No.

32:40.833 --> 32:42.126
I'm bored.

32:42.210 --> 32:45.380
Jeez. You're so clingy
early in the morning.

32:45.964 --> 32:47.382
Come on. Let's hang out.

32:49.926 --> 32:52.720
I'll send you my address. Come over.

32:53.596 --> 32:54.555
Okay.

33:10.989 --> 33:12.031
Fuck!

33:13.783 --> 33:14.617
Damn it! Stop!

33:15.201 --> 33:16.452
You son of a bitch!

34:01.581 --> 34:03.416
Are you all right?

34:04.125 --> 34:05.251
Hey…

34:32.695 --> 34:33.529
What?

34:35.114 --> 34:36.324
Why did you follow me?

34:37.116 --> 34:38.242
Who sent you?

34:40.411 --> 34:42.538
To help.

34:42.622 --> 34:44.957
What? Help who?

34:46.209 --> 34:49.796
I thought that man was being chased…

34:50.713 --> 34:52.840
- Fuck!
- What?

34:52.924 --> 34:54.717
That bastard is an imposter.

34:54.801 --> 34:56.636
- What?
- Mind your own business.

34:56.719 --> 34:59.347
- Okay.
- This fucker, seriously.

35:05.103 --> 35:05.937
What the…

35:35.091 --> 35:36.092
What brings you here?

35:36.175 --> 35:40.138
Mi-yeon's surgery went well yesterday.

35:40.221 --> 35:42.390
Is that so? And how is she now?

35:42.974 --> 35:46.018
Good. She's recovering well.

35:48.271 --> 35:49.939
It's all thanks to you, sir.

35:50.565 --> 35:52.608
If you hadn't helped us,

35:53.109 --> 35:56.237
Mi-yeon might've died.

35:59.323 --> 36:00.158
Here.

36:02.034 --> 36:05.121
Luckily, my husband moved
to a big company recently,

36:05.204 --> 36:07.373
so he received his severance.

36:08.916 --> 36:11.669
I came here
as soon as we received the money

36:11.752 --> 36:14.130
because I wanted to pay you back
before anyone else.

36:17.508 --> 36:19.802
You can take your time paying me back.

36:20.761 --> 36:22.263
Pay off your urgent debts first.

36:22.847 --> 36:26.475
No, sir. Please accept this.

36:27.268 --> 36:29.437
I feel a little at ease now.

36:32.398 --> 36:33.941
Thank you, sir.

36:35.818 --> 36:38.362
Thank you so much.

36:41.073 --> 36:42.241
Thank you.

36:58.716 --> 37:00.927
MI-YEON'S MOTHER APRIL 14TH, 2018
20 MILLION WON

37:06.724 --> 37:10.728
KOREAN ANTIQUE MALL

37:32.708 --> 37:36.629
I found that bastard, Yang Jae-myeong,
but he started bitching about being broke,

37:36.712 --> 37:38.005
so I took this from him.

37:42.051 --> 37:43.928
This is worth over 20 million won.

37:44.011 --> 37:45.054
So what?

37:46.055 --> 37:48.057
Yang Jae-myeong borrowed ten million won.

37:49.100 --> 37:50.101
We got paid with interest.

37:56.148 --> 37:57.191
Did you get hurt?

37:57.275 --> 37:59.735
Fuck. I got in a scuffle
with Yang Jae-myeong.

38:00.736 --> 38:04.448
By the way, we should talk.

38:04.532 --> 38:05.783
Have some rice cakes.

38:06.701 --> 38:09.036
Don't change the subject with rice cakes.

38:11.664 --> 38:12.999
How long are you going to do this?

38:14.417 --> 38:15.251
Do what?

38:17.461 --> 38:19.213
Lend people money with no interest.

38:19.297 --> 38:20.965
It's not profitable.

38:21.465 --> 38:22.633
What do you mean?

38:22.717 --> 38:25.845
I always pay you 30% in commission fees.

38:25.928 --> 38:28.097
Not for me. I mean for you, Grandpa.

38:31.851 --> 38:33.644
You know Mi-yeon's mom, right?

38:34.770 --> 38:35.771
Yes, why?

38:35.855 --> 38:39.358
She dropped by earlier
and paid back everything in cash.

38:41.277 --> 38:42.611
And that's the interest payment?

38:44.613 --> 38:45.531
Hyeon-ju.

38:46.240 --> 38:48.909
A sick child received a timely operation
and regained her health.

38:48.993 --> 38:50.619
Because I lent the family money,

38:50.703 --> 38:53.664
they didn't have to use their home
as collateral and get a loan.

38:53.748 --> 38:57.168
Thanks to that, the child has a home
to return to once she's discharged.

38:58.586 --> 39:00.504
We saved a family.

39:01.339 --> 39:04.633
This is the most valuable form of interest
in the world.

39:07.845 --> 39:08.721
Jeez.

39:08.804 --> 39:12.808
Anyway, I heard this while digging around
for Yang Jae-myeong's whereabouts.

39:12.892 --> 39:16.437
Yang Jae-myeong and his posse
are going around dressed up as homeless

39:16.520 --> 39:19.357
and stealing the real homeless' IDs
to take out loans in their names.

39:19.440 --> 39:20.983
What kind of people are they?

39:21.067 --> 39:24.403
They were in prison with Yang Jae-myeong.
A bunch of thugs.

39:24.487 --> 39:26.447
You knew that, and you still went alone?

39:27.323 --> 39:28.991
Do you want to tag along next time?

39:29.658 --> 39:34.080
Anyway, let me do some digging.
I think I'll find something interesting.

39:34.163 --> 39:35.998
Don't get involved in anything dangerous.

39:36.707 --> 39:37.541
Okay.

39:47.426 --> 39:50.471
PRESIDENT MOON GWANG-MU

39:50.554 --> 39:53.015
MARINE
IF IT DOESN'T WORK, MAKE IT WORK!

39:53.099 --> 39:54.183
Yes, sir.

39:54.266 --> 39:56.060
Hey, am I calling at a bad time?

39:56.560 --> 39:57.770
No, sir. Please go ahead.

39:57.853 --> 40:00.856
Yes, I wanted to ask you a favor.
Find someone for me.

40:00.940 --> 40:02.024
Yes, one moment, please.

40:03.901 --> 40:04.819
Say the word, sir.

40:05.986 --> 40:06.904
"A good person."

40:08.197 --> 40:09.657
"A skilled bodyguard,

40:10.741 --> 40:13.619
even better if they were knowledgeable
about the loan business."

40:16.330 --> 40:17.748
Okay, sir.

40:18.249 --> 40:20.835
I will find the best candidates
as soon as I can.

40:21.419 --> 40:22.753
Thanks for your help.

40:22.837 --> 40:25.214
Yes, sir. Salute!

40:26.715 --> 40:29.051
Mayweather is the top dog.

40:29.135 --> 40:32.471
But Mayweather seems
more like a businessman than a boxer.

40:32.555 --> 40:36.434
That's right. He's in it for the money,
but he is ridiculously good at it.

40:37.143 --> 40:38.936
I'm sure he's made
a few hundred billion won.

40:39.562 --> 40:40.771
Does money matter to you?

40:41.939 --> 40:43.357
What matters more than money?

40:44.066 --> 40:45.192
The heart of a boxer.

40:48.320 --> 40:49.196
What?

40:51.365 --> 40:52.658
What is it?

40:55.995 --> 40:57.997
- Jeez. What?
- Nothing. I'm sorry.

40:58.080 --> 40:59.540
Jeez. Hey.

41:00.082 --> 41:02.585
You just got so serious all of a sudden.

41:02.668 --> 41:04.462
That caught me off guard.

41:04.962 --> 41:06.922
Elaborate on this boxer's heart.

41:07.465 --> 41:08.340
Well…

41:09.508 --> 41:11.927
I think Manny Pacquiao is the best.

41:12.011 --> 41:15.306
Pow! Pow, Pacquiao!

41:15.389 --> 41:18.642
Let me have my moment.
I never cut you off when you are talking.

41:19.393 --> 41:22.605
I'm sorry, Marine sir.
I will never cut you off. Yes!

41:22.688 --> 41:26.942
I really admire Pacquiao's heart.
He never gives up.

41:27.026 --> 41:30.738
I can give him that,
but Mayweather made a lot more money.

41:30.821 --> 41:34.658
But I bet a lot more kids started dreaming
of becoming a boxer because of Pacquiao.

41:34.742 --> 41:36.076
The same goes for me.

41:37.620 --> 41:40.539
This is the kind of person I want to be.

41:40.623 --> 41:43.709
A person who shows
that dreams can come true

41:44.210 --> 41:46.212
if you have a strong will
and undying passion.

41:46.295 --> 41:47.796
It's really windy today.

41:47.880 --> 41:50.007
That is a true boxer's heart

41:50.090 --> 41:54.428
and the kind of hope we should inspire
in the people watching our matches.

41:54.512 --> 41:56.138
- A boxer's--
- Hey, this is ready.

41:56.222 --> 41:57.181
Let's eat.

41:59.350 --> 42:00.184
Here.

42:05.689 --> 42:07.399
- Is it good?
- Yes, it's amazing.

42:08.692 --> 42:10.819
What do you do for a living?

42:10.903 --> 42:15.366
I used to teach gym classes
to kindergartners at my friend's school.

42:15.449 --> 42:16.951
A gym teacher of some sort.

42:17.034 --> 42:18.536
Well, that doesn't suit you.

42:18.619 --> 42:22.414
What do you mean? Kids fucking love me.

42:22.498 --> 42:24.959
I taught in the morning
and trained in the afternoon.

42:25.042 --> 42:27.920
Since the school shut down,
I've been in a bit of a bind.

42:30.297 --> 42:34.301
Do you want to go on deliveries with me?
Parcel delivery is booming.

42:35.177 --> 42:36.637
- Is the pay good?
- Yes.

42:36.720 --> 42:38.305
If we put our minds to it,

42:38.389 --> 42:40.766
we could each make
about 200,000 won per day.

42:40.849 --> 42:41.725
Seriously?

42:41.809 --> 42:43.727
Yes, delivery work is good cardio.

42:43.811 --> 42:47.147
You use muscles you don't use for boxing,
improving your balance.

42:47.231 --> 42:49.441
It's like killing two birds
with one stone. Damn.

42:49.525 --> 42:51.569
- It's three birds.
- How come?

42:51.652 --> 42:54.572
You make money, get your cardio in,
and improve your balance.

42:54.655 --> 42:57.157
Hey, cardio and balance
are counted as one.

42:57.241 --> 42:58.993
No, they are different.

42:59.076 --> 43:00.077
Jeez.

43:00.995 --> 43:04.290
Anyway, weren't you going on
to compete in the Super Series

43:04.373 --> 43:06.709
as the Korean representative
since you won the tournament?

43:06.792 --> 43:10.254
Yes, but it's been postponed indefinitely
due to COVID-19.

43:12.214 --> 43:14.592
How long will that take?

43:15.301 --> 43:16.760
There's nothing I can do about it.

43:19.388 --> 43:23.142
But I'll always be ready to fight.

43:26.186 --> 43:29.773
You seem to have a boxer's heart.

43:37.364 --> 43:38.407
Hey.

43:38.490 --> 43:40.367
- Come on, Pacquiao.
- Right now?

43:41.577 --> 43:42.411
Come on!

43:47.499 --> 43:48.751
Whoa…

43:49.251 --> 43:50.753
Why would you hit me for real?

43:50.836 --> 43:51.962
My bad. I'm sorry.

43:52.046 --> 43:54.715
Hey, come here. Let go.

43:54.798 --> 43:57.885
Come here, Kim Gun-woo!

43:57.968 --> 44:00.054
Hey, Kim Gun-woo! Come here!

44:01.639 --> 44:04.224
Now, cheers!

44:04.933 --> 44:07.603
Drink up!

44:07.686 --> 44:10.939
Today's main event!
The greatest show on Earth!

44:11.023 --> 44:14.276
Cracking a watermelon with In-beom!

44:15.527 --> 44:17.112
Come on! Place your bets!

44:17.196 --> 44:19.073
A million won that he fails!

44:20.115 --> 44:23.243
I bet three million won he succeeds!

44:24.078 --> 44:27.623
If I win this pot, everything's on me!

44:27.706 --> 44:29.249
Beom.

44:29.333 --> 44:32.336
I know you'll crack it,
but I'm betting 4 million that you can't.

44:33.837 --> 44:36.340
- Kang In-beom!
- Let's go!

44:36.423 --> 44:39.134
- Kang In-beom!
- Kang In-beom!

44:39.218 --> 44:41.178
- Let's go!
- Kang In-beom!

44:43.097 --> 44:43.972
He cracked it!

44:46.016 --> 44:47.768
Go eat tteokbokki!

44:47.851 --> 44:49.645
Let's have some tteokbokki!

44:49.728 --> 44:50.813
That was awesome!

44:51.897 --> 44:53.315
I did well, didn't I?

44:53.399 --> 44:54.650
DEAREST MAYOR

44:56.902 --> 44:58.570
Quiet!

45:05.119 --> 45:06.120
Yes, Mr. Mayor.

45:08.580 --> 45:09.415
Yes.

45:12.626 --> 45:13.627
Yes.

45:17.673 --> 45:18.674
Yes, sir.

45:20.175 --> 45:21.385
Yes, I understand.

45:21.468 --> 45:22.761
I will let him know.

45:23.887 --> 45:25.222
Have a good evening, sir.

45:29.101 --> 45:31.770
Our mayor will

45:33.021 --> 45:34.690
back your casino project.

45:43.240 --> 45:46.618
I have prepared a small gift

45:46.702 --> 45:49.288
for your birthday, Mr. Park.

45:54.543 --> 45:55.377
Open it.

46:01.967 --> 46:03.594
It's 3.7 kilograms of gold.

46:04.678 --> 46:09.683
Mr. Park, these turtles are so clean
that no one would know if you took them.

46:10.768 --> 46:12.269
I prepared these in hopes

46:12.352 --> 46:15.272
that our relationship
will continue for a long time.

46:15.355 --> 46:18.692
I would greatly appreciate it
if you accepted them.

46:27.493 --> 46:29.870
Look beyond City Hall.

46:31.371 --> 46:33.415
I know you have big dreams.

46:33.499 --> 46:35.459
If you plan on going to the Blue House

46:35.542 --> 46:38.170
and to the National Assembly,
you will need money.

46:39.338 --> 46:40.881
Let's forge a lasting partnership.

46:41.381 --> 46:43.759
I will support you to the fullest.

46:45.427 --> 46:48.889
My money has never known failure.

47:02.986 --> 47:05.864
Hey!

47:06.365 --> 47:08.283
Hey, where are we going?

47:08.367 --> 47:10.994
Please get in carefully.
We'll take you home.

47:11.078 --> 47:11.912
Let's go.

47:18.460 --> 47:20.587
When will you crack down
on Assemblyman Seo's building?

47:21.088 --> 47:23.257
It differs by store. But by this Friday,

47:23.340 --> 47:26.093
all of them will have accrued
over 20 million in interest.

47:26.593 --> 47:28.512
The small ones will leave
with some convincing.

47:29.179 --> 47:31.139
People tend to give up easier

47:31.223 --> 47:36.436
if they see the ground-floor storefront
in shambles every time they go to work.

47:38.272 --> 47:39.565
I will do as you say, sir.

47:40.816 --> 47:43.485
Since Mr. Jung is not feeling well
and can't come with you,

47:43.569 --> 47:46.363
tell them to send over
about 15 intimidating men.

47:46.446 --> 47:47.573
Beom can wrap things up.

47:48.073 --> 47:49.533
Should we arm them with weapons?

47:50.117 --> 47:54.162
No need.
Tell them to suit up and wear masks.

47:54.246 --> 47:56.415
Sir, I think five should be enough.

47:56.498 --> 47:59.459
I am sure the boss has his reasons.

48:01.461 --> 48:02.713
You're right.

48:03.338 --> 48:04.965
I have made a huge mistake.

48:07.551 --> 48:09.553
You shitheads, there you go again.

48:09.636 --> 48:11.430
Hey, focus. So?

48:12.806 --> 48:13.891
Where do you want to begin?

48:52.846 --> 48:54.848
Oh, hello.

48:55.849 --> 48:57.184
You didn't keep your promise.

48:58.810 --> 48:59.645
What?

48:59.728 --> 49:01.772
You agreed to pay an extension fee

49:02.731 --> 49:04.608
in exchange for a lower interest rate.

49:05.275 --> 49:06.360
What?

49:08.028 --> 49:12.658
You needed to pay the loan extension fee,
which is 10% of the principal,

49:13.241 --> 49:16.787
within 24 hours of signing the contract.
It's part of the contract.

49:16.870 --> 49:19.164
Because you failed
to do such an easy thing,

49:19.790 --> 49:22.501
your extension fee
has accrued 40 million won in interest.

49:22.584 --> 49:26.338
And your credit score has dropped,
so your interest rate is now 20%.

49:27.547 --> 49:32.094
We really started this
with the purest of intentions.

49:33.345 --> 49:35.263
You ruined everything, damn it!

49:37.683 --> 49:39.017
What are you going to do now?

49:39.601 --> 49:41.520
Do you have money to cover the interest?

49:45.232 --> 49:46.650
I will call the police.

49:47.567 --> 49:48.402
The police?

49:50.153 --> 49:51.154
Yes.

50:02.791 --> 50:03.709
Oh my God.

50:11.133 --> 50:12.009
Hey, Mom.

50:12.092 --> 50:13.885
Hey, where are you?

50:13.969 --> 50:15.303
I'm almost there.

50:15.387 --> 50:17.389
Okay, I'm at the café.

50:17.472 --> 50:19.558
A bunch of strange people came over…

50:19.641 --> 50:21.435
Strange people? Who?

50:21.518 --> 50:22.602
Right now…

50:24.730 --> 50:26.189
Mom?

50:42.998 --> 50:44.124
Smash everything!

50:59.222 --> 51:01.183
Who the hell are you, you punk?

51:01.266 --> 51:04.019
Who the hell are you? Get lost, you punk!

51:05.103 --> 51:07.272
Hey! I told you to scram!

51:09.691 --> 51:11.359
This bastard! Hey!

51:13.153 --> 51:15.322
- What's going on? Get him.
- You bastard!

51:15.405 --> 51:18.784
- Who the hell is this punk?
- Hey! You son of a bitch!

51:26.083 --> 51:27.501
Stop that fucker!

51:28.335 --> 51:29.586
That son of a bitch!

51:29.669 --> 51:31.379
- Damn it!
- Fuck!

51:32.422 --> 51:33.840
- Come here.
- Damn it!

51:45.477 --> 51:46.478
You bastard!

51:53.568 --> 51:54.694
You son of a bitch!

52:10.752 --> 52:11.711
You fuck!

52:25.142 --> 52:27.519
- Mom, are you all right?
- Yes.

52:27.602 --> 52:28.728
Are you hurt?

52:28.812 --> 52:30.689
I'm okay.

52:41.449 --> 52:42.367
Who are you?

52:43.827 --> 52:46.037
How dare you do this to our café.

52:47.789 --> 52:48.915
I asked who you are.

53:09.144 --> 53:10.437
Calm down, kid.

53:11.396 --> 53:14.691
Your mother borrowed
some money from our company.

53:16.484 --> 53:17.319
Okay.

53:19.237 --> 53:20.405
What do you want?

53:21.698 --> 53:22.908
Pay back what you owe.

53:23.491 --> 53:25.327
Pay for the damages to our café first.

53:47.098 --> 53:48.183
Beom.

53:59.527 --> 54:01.863
Mom, it's okay.
Go over there for a second.

54:01.947 --> 54:02.948
Gun-woo.

55:20.692 --> 55:21.609
Gun-woo!

55:50.013 --> 55:51.848
Gun-woo, no!

56:10.241 --> 56:11.076
Beom.

56:35.016 --> 56:38.978
I like people with grit.

56:40.855 --> 56:44.442
- Damn it.
- Guys with grit can get anything done.

56:47.695 --> 56:48.863
Want to work for me?

56:49.364 --> 56:50.490
I will…

59:25.770 --> 59:28.731
Subtitle translation by:
